messages.text:
Good points all. Let me clarify:
@560411: The line supervisor is responsible for the handoff. I'll make that explicit in A2.
@18383: Excellent suggestion. I'll add an electrical/mechanical triage step right after the initial alert validation.
@237177: The maintenance technician who completes the work is responsible for closing the work order and updating the log. I'll add that to the 'Resolution' phase of the process.

@36422 I estimate about 3-4 hours per asset, including wiring and testing. It should fit comfortably within a standard maintenance shift.
@237177 No special tools required, just standard electrical hand tools. Your team should be well-equipped.
@53841 Yes, I've selected cost-effective but reliable sensors. The total cost is well within our allocated budget.
